Third-party material included in this product
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Keccak-f[1600] permutation (src/kem.rs, examples/kyber_benchmark.rs)
   Translated to Rust from the eXtended Keccak Code Package (XKCP),
   https://github.com/XKCP/XKCP, files KeccakP-1600-opt64.c,
   KeccakP-1600-64.macros and KeccakP-1600-unrolling.macros, by the Keccak
   team (Guido Bertoni, Joan Daemen, Seth Hoffert, Michaël Peeters, Gilles
   Van Assche, Ronny Van Keer). Released by its authors to the public domain
   (CC0 1.0 Universal).

2. Kyber / ML-KEM reference structure and constants (src/kem.rs, src/ntt.rs,
   examples/kyber_benchmark.rs)
   The int16 Montgomery NTT structure, the twiddle-factor table ZETAS, the
   Barrett and Montgomery reduction constants, the compression and message
   decoding formulas and the CBD samplers follow the pq-crystals Kyber
   reference implementation, https://github.com/pq-crystals/kyber, by the
   CRYSTALS-Kyber team (Roberto Avanzi, Joppe Bos, Léo Ducas, Eike Kiltz,
   Tancrède Lepoint, Vadim Lyubashevsky, John M. Schanck, Peter Schwabe,
   Gregor Seiler, Damien Stehlé). Licensed under CC0 1.0 Universal or the
   Apache License, Version 2.0, at the user's option.

3. NIST ACVP test vectors (tests/kat/)
   Extracted from https://github.com/usnistgov/ACVP-Server,
   gen-val/json-files/ML-KEM-keyGen-FIPS203 and ML-KEM-encapDecap-FIPS203,
   by tests/kat/extract.mjs. A work of the United States Government, not
   subject to copyright protection in the United States (17 U.S.C. § 105).
   NIST provides it without warranty; the vector files record their source.

4. Algorithm
   ML-KEM is specified in NIST FIPS 203 (August 2024). This product
   implements the specification; it has not been validated under FIPS 140-3
   (CMVP) or any other scheme. No patent assurances are given beyond those in
   Section 3 of the Apache License.

